{"content":[{"c":["HELKATH-HAZZURIM*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Area near the pool of Gibeon, where 12 champions from Joab’s army and 12 from Abner’s battled. All 24 died in the fight, each fighter killing his opponent (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.2.16","r":"2Sam.2.16","rawR":"2Sam.2.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.2.16","value":"2Sam.2.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 2:16"},"). Some scholars think the name may mean “field of the crafty,” that is, “field of ambush” or “field of the adversaries.” The ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," renders it “the Field of Swords” (mg)."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"HelkathHazzurim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 2:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.2.16","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.2.16","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.2.16"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"4e54a103571e7949cb1c64a6b76d2905407df77790d534320add43df0ece1d43","sourceItemName":"HelkathHazzurim","sourceItemOrder":232,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"HelkathHazzurim","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Helkath-Hazzurim*","title":"Helkath-Hazzurim*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}